  "report": "Only the initial stage is supplied; a second-stage diagnosis is unavailable. This assessment covers the 19 focal records, all comments on one brand TikTok video. No video body or context-only records are supplied. Unnamed packaging cannot be assigned to a specific SKU or version.\n\nPackaging reception is favorable across distinct visible accounts: metal styling, cuteness, packaging care and refillability attract praise. P00’s chic/environmentally friendly statement has 296 displayed likes; P15’s planned reuse of an empty for medication has 150. These are audience resonance, not verified experiences or buying effects. Broad aesthetic approval recurs across accounts in this single thread; environmental performance does not receive equivalent corroboration. P01 is brand agreement, P03 is P00’s same-author qualified explanation, and P02 questions recyclability. P03’s component-level speculation is not verification. P26 praises packaging while asking what the product does for skin; this limits any inference from packaging enthusiasm to efficacy satisfaction.\n\nThe precise failure proposition—an unidentified product arrived leaking with a loose top—is supported by one detailed customer account, P06 (12 likes). The customer opened and cleaned it and worried about oxygen exposure. Neither product damage nor a general mechanical cause is established. P07, the brand’s reply (12 likes), says short exposure is not an issue and offers a replacement after email contact. This corroborates the service offer, not an independent customer experience or independently verified safety. No additional arrival-leak agreement, retailer leak, replacement shipment or delivery appears in the supplied records. There is no observed opposition to this individual incident, but recurrence and prevalence remain unestablished. Positive reception and a failure report coexist without demonstrating that the same package or version received both judgments.\n\nExplicit consequences remain differentiated: P17 reports an all-Experiment routine and Continuum in transit, demonstrating stated loyalty and an acquisition underway without attributing either to packaging. P20 expresses broad buying enthusiasm, without confirmed checkout. P32 conditionally considers saving up; P38 anticipates trying the product. P42 reports receipt that day and newly discovered refillability, without evidence that refillability motivated acquisition. P04 and P27 request refill bundles; neither establishes purchase or repurchase intent. P15 proposes reuse, rather than reporting completed reuse. P29 asks about a sticker in a refill, with the precise concern unresolved. No focal account explicitly reports future repeat purchase, abandonment, refund, or fulfilled replacement. Complaint-to-loyalty effects are unknown because the complaint and loyalty statements belong to different accounts.\n\nAll engagement values are displayed likes observed 2026-09-09T11:56:25.935Z; publication labels show month-day without year. Values are preserved below. The capture reports 47 displayed bodies against 72 advertised comments, but only these 19 focal records are available here. Expanded arrival-leak and metal-packaging branches do not establish completeness; other branches remain outside scope. Native comment IDs are unavailable. P00/P03 share an author, and P01/P07 share the brand author; source-account counts below are keyed records, not independent-origin or event counts. There is no cross-venue corroboration in this supplied stage.",
  "source_index": [
    {
      "key": "P00",
      "findings": "@randomdude7551, TikTok 5-15; 296 likes. Calls unidentified metal packaging chic and environmentally friendly. Strong visible resonance for the combined statement; environmental benefit remains unverified. Same author as P03; no buying consequence."
    },
    {
      "key": "P01",
      "findings": "@experimentwrld, brand/creator reply to P00, 5-15; 39 likes. Bare emphatic agreement with P00, not independent customer corroboration or environmental verification. Same brand author as P07."
    },
    {
      "key": "P02",
      "findings": "@person1234567556987, reply to P00, 5-15; 0 likes. Questions environmental friendliness and recyclability. Preserves skepticism rather than establishing non-recyclability; unidentified product."
    },
    {
      "key": "P03",
      "findings": "@randomdude7551, reply under P00, 5-15; 2 likes. Says aluminum is almost always recyclable, inner part likely recyclable, pump likely not, and pump/shell reusable. Qualified assertions without verification; repeats P00’s origin, not an additional independent endorsement."
    },
    {
      "key": "P04",
      "findings": "@flamingpanda5, reply under P00, 5-20; 0 likes. Requests refill bundles for unspecified products. Desired offering, not completed purchase or explicit repeat-purchase intent."
    },
    {
      "key": "P06",
      "findings": "@jasminesingh1102, 5-15; 12 likes. Reports unidentified product arriving leaked with loose top, requiring opening and cleaning; asks whether oxygen exposure makes it unusable. One detailed arrival-leak/loose-top report; damage, SKU/version and subsequent use unknown."
    },
    {
      "key": "P07",
      "findings": "@experimentwrld, brand/creator reply to P06, 5-16; 12 likes. Says short-term exposure is not an issue and offers replacement after contacting hey@experimentbeauty.com. Offer only: no evidence of contact, dispatch or delivery; reassurance is brand-owned."
    },
    {
      "key": "P15",
      "findings": "@bmdubs, 5-15; 150 likes. Plans to use an empty unidentified package to hold Lexapro. Resonant reuse intention, not completed reuse, validated storage suitability or evidence of repurchase."
    },
    {
      "key": "P17",
      "findings": "@mostlyconceptual, 5-16; 1 like. Reports unusually strong brand loyalty, an all-Experiment skincare routine, and Continuum in the mail. Routine’s other SKUs and versions unknown; no packaging attribution or explicit repeat-purchase intent."
    },
    {
      "key": "P20",
      "findings": "@countryboiiloveyouuuxoxo, 5-15; 7 likes. Says “I’m buying everrrrrything from yall!” Broad buying enthusiasm/declaration; specific products, completed checkout and packaging motivation unconfirmed."
    },
    {
      "key": "P21",
      "findings": "@beautybought, 5-17; 1 like. Praises consistently amazing products and packaging customers can feel good about. Brand-wide approval without specific SKU, verified environmental attribute or buying consequence; promotional relationship unavailable."
    },
    {
      "key": "P26",
      "findings": "@adam_thomas6, 5-21; 1 like. Calls packaging great but asks what it does for skin. Aesthetic approval alongside unresolved efficacy interest, not reported efficacy failure or use."
    },
    {
      "key": "P27",
      "findings": "@sofieeee120, 5-24; 1 like. Requests a bundle of Continuum and Super Saturated refills. Named two-product offering interest, not evidence of joint use, acquisition or intended repurchase."
    },
    {
      "key": "P29",
      "findings": "@allthegr8namesaretaken, 5-17; 2 likes. Asks how to get the sticker in their refill. Unspecified product and unresolved sticker-related question; no demonstrated defect or purchase consequence."
    },
    {
      "key": "P32",
      "findings": "@josemarbp, 5-18; 3 likes. Calls the unidentified offering genius and says they might need to save up. Conditional interest with a possible affordability constraint, not completed buying."
    },
    {
      "key": "P38",
      "findings": "@taylorelissa, 5-16; 1 like. Calls package cute and anticipates trying it. Packaging approval and trial intention; acquisition, use and product identity unconfirmed."
    },
    {
      "key": "P39",
      "findings": "@morco11111, 5-29; 1 like. Praises the brand for treating packaging as seriously as formulas. Perceived packaging care, without specific product, comparative performance or buying evidence."
    },
    {
      "key": "P40",
      "findings": "@danaisabellaaa, 5-15; 1 like. Bare “SOOOO CUTE” approval in the packaging discussion. Supports contextual aesthetic reception only; specific referent and experience unknown."
    },
    {
      "key": "P42",
      "findings": "@__whitneyjade, 5-20; 1 like. Reports receiving the unidentified product that day and excitement at discovering it is refillable. Receipt and newfound awareness, not refill purchase, completed reuse or evidence that refillability motivated acquisition."
    }
